title: Move a minister
new-page: true

= Move a minister

Choose a department, then its new minister. Each change pleases one wing of the party and annoys the other. A minister who already holds a post must be replaced there before moving. The Cabinet is now [+ cabinet_dry +]% dry.

- @move_treasury
- @move_employment
- @move_industry
- @move_home
- @move_foreign
- @move_environment
- @move_defence
- @move_education
- @move_health
- @done: Finish the reshuffle.

@done
call: cabinet_recalc
go-to: root

@move_treasury
title: The Treasury
subtitle: Now: [+ chancellor +] ([+ chancellor_dry : drywet +]).

**Chancellor of the Exchequer.** The Budget, taxes, spending and, with the Bank of England, interest rates. At present the post is held by [+ chancellor +].

- @appoint_treasury_howe
- @appoint_treasury_lawson
- @appoint_treasury_pym
- @ministers: Choose another department.

@appoint_treasury_howe
title: Sir Geoffrey Howe
subtitle: Dry. The architect of our economic policy.
view-if: chancellor != "Howe" and employment_secretary != "Howe" and industry_secretary != "Howe" and home_secretary != "Howe" and foreign_secretary != "Howe" and environment_secretary != "Howe" and defence_secretary != "Howe" and education_secretary != "Howe" and health_secretary != "Howe"
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 4 if chancellor_dry = 0; dry_dissent -= 3 if chancellor_dry = 0; cabinet_revolt -= 1 if chancellor_dry = 0; loyalist_dissent -= 1 if chancellor_dry = 1; chancellor = "Howe"; chancellor_dry = 1
call: cabinet_recalc
go-to: ministers

Sir Geoffrey Howe becomes Chancellor of the Exchequer.

@appoint_treasury_lawson
title: Nigel Lawson
subtitle: Dry. A combative monetarist who thinks he could run the Treasury better than anyone.
view-if: chancellor != "Lawson" and employment_secretary != "Lawson" and industry_secretary != "Lawson" and home_secretary != "Lawson" and foreign_secretary != "Lawson" and environment_secretary != "Lawson" and defence_secretary != "Lawson" and education_secretary != "Lawson" and health_secretary != "Lawson"
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 4 if chancellor_dry = 0; dry_dissent -= 3 if chancellor_dry = 0; cabinet_revolt -= 1 if chancellor_dry = 0; loyalist_dissent -= 1 if chancellor_dry = 1; chancellor = "Lawson"; chancellor_dry = 1
call: cabinet_recalc
go-to: ministers

Nigel Lawson becomes Chancellor of the Exchequer.

@appoint_treasury_pym
title: Francis Pym
subtitle: Wet. A patrician pessimist and a safe pair of hands.
view-if: chancellor != "Pym" and employment_secretary != "Pym" and industry_secretary != "Pym" and home_secretary != "Pym" and foreign_secretary != "Pym" and environment_secretary != "Pym" and defence_secretary != "Pym" and education_secretary != "Pym" and health_secretary != "Pym"
on-arrival: dry_dissent += 4 if chancellor_dry = 1; wet_dissent -= 3 if chancellor_dry = 1; cabinet_revolt -= 1 if chancellor_dry = 1; loyalist_dissent -= 1 if chancellor_dry = 0; chancellor = "Pym"; chancellor_dry = 0
call: cabinet_recalc
go-to: ministers

Francis Pym becomes Chancellor of the Exchequer.

