#################### The purge, one department at a time

@purge_start
title: Sack the wets
subtitle: Take control of the Cabinet, one department at a time.
view-if: wets_purged = 0
on-arrival: purge_count = 0
go-to: purge_employment

@purge_employment
title: Employment
go-to: purge_education if employment_dry = 1 or tebbit_elsewhere = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.tebbit_elsewhere = 0;
for (var v of ['chancellor', 'industry_secretary', 'home_secretary', 'foreign_secretary', 'environment_secretary', 'defence_secretary', 'education_secretary', 'health_secretary']) {
    if (Q[v] == 'Tebbit') {
        Q.tebbit_elsewhere = 1;
    }
}
!}

**Employment.** [+ employment_secretary +] has resisted every attempt to strip the unions of their legal immunities.

- @purge_prior
- @purge_keep_employment

@purge_prior
title: Move the Employment Secretary to Northern Ireland, and give Employment to Norman Tebbit.
subtitle: The unions lose their friend in Cabinet. The wets lose their leader.
on-arrival: purge_count += 1; employment_secretary = "Tebbit"; employment_dry = 1; wet_dissent += 5; dry_dissent -= 3; union_power -= 2
go-to: purge_education

The Employment Secretary protests, threatens to resign, and goes to Belfast anyway. Norman Tebbit takes over at Employment.

@purge_keep_employment
title: Leave Employment as it is.
go-to: purge_education

@purge_education
title: Education
go-to: purge_grandees if education_dry = 1

**Education.** [+ education_secretary +] has fought every cut to the schools budget.

- @purge_carlisle_joseph
- @purge_carlisle_boyson
- @purge_keep_education

@purge_carlisle_joseph
title: Sack the Education Secretary, and send Sir Keith Joseph to Education.
subtitle: Patrick Jenkin takes over at Industry, and Norman Fowler at Health and Social Security.
view-if: industry_secretary == "Joseph"
on-arrival: purge_count += 1; education_secretary = "Joseph"; education_dry = 1; industry_secretary = "Jenkin"; industry_dry = 1; health_dry = 1 if health_secretary == "Jenkin"; health_secretary = "Fowler" if health_secretary == "Jenkin"; wet_dissent += 4; dry_dissent -= 2
go-to: purge_grandees

Sir Keith moves to Education, where he hopes to bring choice to the schools. Patrick Jenkin goes to Industry and Norman Fowler to the DHSS.

@purge_carlisle_boyson
title: Sack the Education Secretary, and promote Rhodes Boyson.
view-if: industry_secretary != "Joseph" and chancellor != "Boyson" and home_secretary != "Boyson" and foreign_secretary != "Boyson" and environment_secretary != "Boyson" and defence_secretary != "Boyson" and health_secretary != "Boyson"
on-arrival: purge_count += 1; education_secretary = "Boyson"; education_dry = 1; wet_dissent += 4; dry_dissent -= 2
go-to: purge_grandees

Rhodes Boyson, a former headmaster and the scourge of progressive education, takes over at Education.

@purge_keep_education
title: Leave Education as it is.
go-to: purge_grandees

@purge_grandees
title: The grandees

**The grandees.** Sir Ian Gilmour, the Lord Privy Seal, and Lord Soames, the Leader of the Lords, speak for the wets in every Cabinet argument. Neither runs a big department, so sacking them is a matter of authority, not policy.

- @purge_gilmour_soames
- @purge_keep_grandees

@purge_gilmour_soames
title: Sack Sir Ian Gilmour and Lord Soames.
subtitle: A signal to the whole party. The wets will not forgive it.
on-arrival: purge_count += 1; wet_dissent += 6; wet_strength -= 3; rebellion += 1; n_advisors -= 1 if gilmour_advisor = 1; gilmour_advisor = 0
achievement: full_speed_ahead
go-to: purge_done

Soames is furious and says so to your face. Gilmour tells the cameras outside Number 10: "It does no harm to throw the occasional man overboard, but it does not do much good if you are steering full speed ahead for the rocks."

@purge_keep_grandees
title: Leave them in place.
go-to: purge_done

@purge_done
title: The new Cabinet
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.purge_count >= 2) {
    Q.wets_purged = 1;
    this.achieve('purge');
}
Q.cabinet_revolt = Math.max(0, Q.cabinet_revolt - 3 * Q.purge_count);
Q.dry_dissent -= 2 * Q.purge_count;
!}
call: cabinet_recalc

[? if purge_count >= 2 : The Cabinet is yours now. The newspapers call it the night of the long knives, and the wets on the backbenches start to talk to each other in corridors. ?][? if purge_count = 1 : A limited reshuffle: the wets are warned, not routed. ?][? if purge_count = 0 : In the end you change nothing. The wets conclude that you didn't dare. ?] The Cabinet is now [+ cabinet_dry +]% dry.

- @root: Continue.
